From cf51c49838e678e4f3bc792f2e1e9b51895c0470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jocelyn Lin <jocelyn.lin@workday.com>
Date: Tue, 5 May 2026 18:51:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(observe,server): support filtering executions by
 multiple agentflow IDs

Server (packages/server):
- GET /executions agentflowId query accepts any HTTP idiom: single,
  comma-separated, repeated keys, or a mix; all flatten into a string[]
- Service uses a single IN (:...agentflowIds) clause for both single and
  multi cases; single-id callers preserved (wire format unchanged)

SDK (@flowiseai/observe):
- ExecutionsViewerProps and ExecutionFilters take agentflowIds: string[]
- API client serializes to canonical comma-joined form for wire-format
  stability regardless of axios paramsSerializer

Example app:
- VITE_FLOW_IDS env var (one or comma-separated UUIDs)
- Demo header surfaces multi-agentflow scope

Tests:
- New controllers/executions/index.test.ts covers all four wire shapes
  plus whitespace and empty-input edge cases
- API client tests for comma-joined serialization + empty-array omission

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
